In article <6090@ccncsu.ColoState.EDU> ja802891@longs.LANCE.ColoState.EDU (jennifer archie) writes:
>Can anyone tell me if there is a way to unlock chests, using a key that
>is not explicitly for them? I had a key with no particular shape and
>I tried to apply it to the locked chest and it gave an error message of
>no door being present. Hmmm.
>
You need to stand on the location where the chest is and 'a'pply the key
downward ( '>' ). Some named keys are just keys; some are skeleton keys.
Only skeleton keys open doors so you can identify them this way. Lock picks
always work but take more time. Credit cards unlock but do not lock things.

To open a chest without a matching key, skeleton key or lock pick you can 
either #force it (again, you must be standing over it) with a weapon or
pick-axe, or kick it ( ^D ) in which case you have to stand NEXT to it and
kick in that direction, like when you kick a door in. I find that kicking 
is better; it takes a couple of turns tops for mediocre characters while
forcing takes a long time with less chance of success and your character
won't stop sometimes until a monster hits. Also, if you are trying to 
#force a chest, use a non-edged weapon, e.g. mace, flail, bullwhip. 
Any weapon used to pry has a chance of breaking; bashing-type weapons
don't.


